     "subject": "HPO-26-00629 lines 10 and 20 - revised dates and laminate allocation",
     "body": "Dear Huang Shu-fen,\n\nThank you for your note of 16 September on the longer multilayer lead time. Please confirm the following on HPO-26-00629:\n\n1. Line 10 (HR-30110, 830 pcs), moved from 25 September to 16 October, and line 20 (HR-30120, 950 pcs), moved from 28 September to 19 October. Are these dates firm? Please confirm both parts are 6 layers or more, and that the 2-layer and 4-layer parts on our orders are unaffected.\n2. How much of your high-Tg FR-4 laminate allocation is committed to Halden, and for which weeks?\n3. Could the quick-turn service hold the original dates for these two lines? Please tell us what it would cover, but we are not asking you to proceed on it yet.\n4. The attachment quotation LXC-QT-26-0412 did not come through readable on our side. Please re-send it as a readable document showing the unit, validity date, minimum order and the volume basis for 2027.\n\nPlease reply as soon as you can. This is a request for information only and does not change the order or commit Halden to anything, and Halden's rights under the order are unchanged.\n\nBest regards,\nHalden Robotics Procurement"
